    "body": "## Motivation\n\nin speculative decoding, multiple draft tokens get committed to output_ids before finish checks run. when a request gets aborted mid-run via to_finish, update_finish_state sets finished_reason and returns early without setting finished_len or checking length boundaries. because finished_len stayed none, output_ids_through_stop returned the raw output_ids including the overshot speculative tokens, so completion_tokens exceeded max_new_tokens on aborted requests (issue #44839).\n\n## Modifications\n\nclamps finished_len to max_new_tokens inside the to_finish handler when output_ids meets or exceeds the cap, and ensures output_ids_through_stop and the output streamer never emit past max_new_tokens. added unit tests covering speculative aborts both over and under the token cap in test_finish_length_speculative.py.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39210363171](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39210363171)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39210363104](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39210363104)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39210363105](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39210363105)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
